{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["Great plenty (שָׂבָע גדול) — it is all with qamatz, for its accent is below (on the final syllable), and it is a noun, like: דָבָר, בָּקָר, רָעָב. And from among these one says דְּבָרְךָ בְּקָרְךָ and so forth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The accent 'below' refers to milra (stress on the final syllable), which for certain noun patterns produces qamatz in all syllables. The final example illustrates segholate nouns in the construct state."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:55.411501652Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}